message.content:
Fix two issues in the Zip Code Checker Shopify app:

**Issue #2: Widget visible in Theme Editor when app embed is disabled**
File: `extensions/zip-code-widget/blocks/zip-code-checker.liquid`

Currently the `{% if request.design_mode %}` block shows a full mock widget preview. When the app embed is toggled OFF in Theme Editor > App Embeds, this preview still shows, confusing merchants.

Fix: Replace the design_mode block to use JavaScript to check `window.__zccAppEnabled`. Show two states:
- If app embed is enabled: show the current beautiful preview
- If app embed is NOT enabled: show a compact card that says "Zip Code Checker — Enable the app embed in App Embeds to activate this widget" with a subtle border

Here's the approach - wrap the existing preview HTML in a container, and add a small script that checks `__zccAppEnabled` after a short delay (the app embed script may not have loaded yet):

```liquid
{% if request.design_mode %}
  <div id="zcc-editor-{{ block.id }}">
    <!-- Inactive state (shown by default) -->
    <div id="zcc-inactive-{{ block.id }}" style="
      background:#f6f6f7;border:1px dashed #c9cccf;border-radius:8px;
      padding:16px;max-width:480px;text-align:center;
      font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,sans-serif;
      color:#6d7175;font-size:13px;
    ">
      <p style="margin:0 0 4px;font-weight:600;color:#202223;">Zip Code Checker</p>
      <p style="margin:0;">Enable the app embed in <strong>App Embeds</strong> to activate this widget.</p>
    </div>
    <!-- Active preview (hidden by default, shown when app embed is active) -->
    <div id="zcc-active-{{ block.id }}" style="display:none;">
      [PUT THE EXISTING PREVIEW HTML HERE - the full mock widget with the green success state]
    </div>
  </div>
  <script>
  (function() {
    var bid = "{{ block.id }}";
    function check() {
      if (window.__zccAppEnabled) {
        var inactive = document.getElementById('zcc-inactive-' + bid);
        var active = document.getElementById('zcc-active-' + bid);
        if (inactive) inactive.style.display = 'none';
        if (active) active.style.display = 'block';
      }
    }
    // Check immediately and after delays (app embed may load later)
    check();
    setTimeout(check, 500);
    setTimeout(check, 1500);
    setTimeout(check, 3000);
  })();
  </script>
{% else %}
```

Keep all the existing non-design-mode code (the `{% else %}` branch) exactly as-is. Only modify the `{% if request.design_mode %}` branch.

**Issue #6: Redesign Help & Support page**
File: `app/routes/app.help.tsx`

Read the current file first, then redesign the support section at the bottom. Requirements:
1. Add a "Support Hours" card showing:
   - Monday - Friday: 9 AM - 6 PM IST
   - Saturday: 10 AM - 4 PM IST
   - Sunday: Closed
   - "We typically respond within 2-4 hours"
2. Replace the current support buttons section with a cleaner "Still need help?" card with: Documentation, Email Support, Feature Requests buttons
3. Use ONLY Polaris components (Card, BlockStack, InlineStack, Text, Button, Badge, Divider, Banner, Icon)
4. Keep all existing FAQ content exactly as-is — only change the support/contact section at the bottom

Do NOT add a live chat button (requires external service integration we don't have).

Run `npm run typecheck` after all changes.
